2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Kebab case repos snake case local checkouts
 # uuid: a184e9d8-85b8-50db-9211-d6fa0475fec4
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Prediscussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Repo names are kebab-case on GitHub, and local checkouts keep the names the build expects.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Repositories across our orgs grew inconsistent names. The loot-action slice under `v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric` mixed kebab-case (`combat-core`, `loot-core`) with snake_case (`entity_packet`), and the `sinew-mocap` org carried `mount_drift` and `vr_bridge` alongside kebab-case peers.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Check a repository with `gh repo list <org>`, which shows no repository name matching `[_A-Z]`.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Kebab case repos snake case local checkouts
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2064) 'See `DETAILS.md` for the full argument.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2064) 'See `DETAILS.md` for the full argument.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2064) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2064) 'We want one repo-naming convention so clones, links, and code search stay predictable.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Context and problem statement
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Repositories across our orgs grew inconsistent names. The loot-action slice under `v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric` mixed kebab-case (`combat-core`, `loot-core`) with snake_case (`entity_packet`), and the `sinew-mocap` org carried `mount_drift` and `vr_bridge` alongside kebab-case peers. We want one repo-naming convention so clones, links, and code search stay predictable.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2064) 'The complication is that several C++ repos are consumed as siblings _by directory path_. `solve/CMakeLists.txt` does `add_subdirectory(../mount_drift …)`, CI workflows in `solve`, `viewer`, and `packaging` check the repo out to `path: mount_drift`, and the homebrew formula stages a `mount_drift` resource to `../mount_drift`. Renaming the local checkout directory to kebab-case would break every one of those hardcoded paths. So: what should repos be named, and must the local checkout directory match the repo name?
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Decision drivers
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Repo names should be uniform and discoverable across orgs.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2064) '- The convention must not break build wiring that hardcodes sibling directory paths.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Language-native package identifiers (Lean, C++) are snake_case; local dirs that feed the build should respect that.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Renaming a GitHub repo is low-risk: GitHub serves automatic redirects from the old name, so existing clone URLs and CI checkouts keep working.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Considered options
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Kebab-case everywhere, both GitHub repos and local checkout directories.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2064) '- snake_case everywhere.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Kebab-case GitHub repos; local checkout directories keep build-native names.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Decision outcome
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Chosen option: "Kebab-case GitHub repos; local checkout directories keep build-native names", because it gives uniform remote naming while preserving the directory names that CMake, CI, and packaging reference as siblings.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2064) 'The rules:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2064) '- GitHub repository names are kebab-case, for example `combat-core`, `loot-core`, `entity-packet`, `mount-drift`, and `vr-bridge`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Local checkout directory names match what the build expects. Where a repo is consumed as a sibling by path (`add_subdirectory(../mount_drift)`, a CI `path:`, a homebrew `resource`), the local directory keeps the snake_case name the build hardcodes, so local `mount_drift` maps to remote `sinew-mocap/mount-drift`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Where no build path depends on the directory name, the local directory may match the kebab-case repo name. The loot-action slice directories were renamed to kebab-case on this basis (`combat-core`, `loot-core`, `entity-packet`, and the rest).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Old remote URLs keep working through GitHub redirects. Update `origin` URLs at convenience, and leave the hardcoded `repository:` and `resource` strings that already resolve through the redirect.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Consequences
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Good: remote names are uniform and code search / links are predictable.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Good: a rename is just `gh repo rename` plus a local `git remote set-url`; CI that still clones the old name keeps working through the redirect.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Good: no build breakage, sibling-by-path repos retain the directory name the build hardcodes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Bad: a local directory name can differ from its remote repo name (`mount_drift` ↔ `mount-drift`), which can surprise newcomers.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Bad: fully propagating kebab-case into the build files (CMake, CI, homebrew) would require coordinated multi-repo PRs through the merge queue; that is deliberately out of scope here.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Confirmation
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2064) '- `gh repo list <org>` shows no repository name matching `[_A-Z]`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2064) '- Repos consumed as siblings by path keep their snake_case checkout directory, and `add_subdirectory(../mount_drift)` still resolves locally.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2064) '- For `sinew-mocap`: `mount_drift` → `sinew-mocap/mount-drift` and `vr_bridge` → `sinew-mocap/vr-bridge` were renamed on GitHub; the local checkout directories remain `mount_drift` and `vr_bridge`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2064) 'More information
 # tags: rfd:madr-heading
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2064) 'Relates to the org split that created `v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric` and to the GHCR package-ownership decision; both concern how repositories are organized and referenced. See `decisions/20260606-org-split-v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric.md` and `rfd/2009-ghcr-package-ownership-same-repo`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2064  1 LINE
 Text:Written
